# Microsoft Fabric Development Rules

> **Updates**: These instructions do not run a session-start update check. Refresh them through your host's plugin or marketplace update flow, or run `git pull` if you use a manual clone.

## Context
This project works with Microsoft Fabric for data engineering, warehousing, and analytics.
Primary API reference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/rest/api/fabric/articles/

## Architecture Mode
- Follow repository layering: Agents -> Skills -> Common.
- For medallion and other cross-endpoint workflows, start with `agents/FabricDataEngineer.agent.md`.
- Delegate endpoint-specific tasks to corresponding skills in `skills/`.

## Authentication
All operations require Azure AD tokens via `az login`:
```bash
az login
az account get-access-token --resource https://api.fabric.microsoft.com
```

## Developer Pattern: REST + Protocol
Developers use REST APIs to manage artifacts, then protocol-specific connections to access data:
- REST → ODBC for Warehouse
- REST → Spark for Lakehouse
- REST → XMLA/DAX for Semantic Models
- REST → KQL for Real-Time Intelligence

## Code Generation Rules

### Lakehouse & Spark
- Always use Delta Lake format for tables
- Use mssparkutils for Fabric-specific operations (fs, credentials, notebook)
- Include partition columns for large tables
- Run OPTIMIZE and VACUUM for table maintenance
- Use `skills/spark-cli/SKILL.md` for notebook authoring and runs, Livy analysis, Spark diagnostics, and the full Materialized Lake View lifecycle.
- MLV authoring resources: `skills/spark-cli/references/authoring/resources/materialized-lake-view-patterns.md` and `skills/spark-cli/references/authoring/resources/mlv-incremental-refresh-patterns.md`.

### Warehouse (T-SQL)
- Check T-SQL surface area - not all SQL Server features are supported
- Use CTAS for large transformations
- Prefer stored procedures for reusable logic
- Always include TOP/LIMIT when exploring data
- Skill: `skills/sqldw-cli/SKILL.md` - one skill with authoring, consumption and operations modes

### SQL Database (in Fabric, OLTP)
- OLTP database with an enforced T-SQL surface (PK/FK/constraints), Query Store, and DMVs - distinct from the Warehouse
- Connect over TDS with `sqlcmd` to the SQL database (read-write) endpoint, not the SQL analytics endpoint, for authoring and diagnostics
- Skill: `skills/sqldb-cli/SKILL.md` — one mode dispatcher; `authoring` for DDL/DML, constraints and indexes, `consumption` for read-only T-SQL, `operations` for Query Store / DMV diagnostics

### Notebooks
- Tag first cell as "parameters" for parameterized notebooks
- Use mssparkutils.credentials.getSecret() for secrets
- Structure with clear markdown headers

### Pipelines
- Use expressions for dynamic content: @pipeline().parameters.Name
- Implement error handling with failure activities
- Add retry policies for transient failures

### KQL (Real-Time Intelligence)
- Always include time filters: `where Timestamp > ago(1h)`
- Use `has` over `contains` for indexed term search
- Use `summarize` with `bin()` for time-series aggregations
- Prefer materialized views for frequent aggregation queries
- Use `.create-merge table` and `.create-or-alter function` for idempotent schema deployment
- Primary CLI tool: `az rest` against the Kusto REST API (see eventhouse skills for patterns)
- Unified skill: `skills/eventhouse-cli/SKILL.md` with authoring and consumption modes

### Spark Operations
- Spark skill: `skills/spark-cli/SKILL.md` — read-only triage for failed jobs, stuck sessions, and performance bottlenecks

### Azure Monitor Observability (Real-Time Intelligence)
- Operations skill: `skills/azmon-mirroredcatalogs-operations-cli/SKILL.md` — onboard Azure Monitor / App Insights / Log Analytics observability data into Fabric and correlate telemetry with business data for business-impact insights, an optional Real-Time (KQL) dashboard, and opt-in Operations Agent instructions

### Dataflows Gen2 (Data Integration)
- Use Fabric REST API for dataflow lifecycle management and Power Query M mashup authoring
- Primary CLI tool: `az rest` against the Fabric REST API
- Dataflows skill: `skills/dataflows-cli/SKILL.md` (authoring and consumption are modes)

### Eventstreams (Real-Time Intelligence)
- Create and manage Eventstream topologies via Fabric REST API
- Supports 25 source types, 8 operators (Filter, Aggregate, GroupBy, SQL, etc.), 4 destination types
- Node names must be alphanumeric PascalCase, 3-63 characters
- Primary CLI tool: `az rest` against the Fabric REST API
- Eventstream skill: `skills/eventstream-cli/SKILL.md` (authoring and consumption are modes)

### Event Schema Sets (Real-Time Intelligence)
- Catalogs of event types and message schemas, accessed via the Fabric Items REST API (`.../eventSchemaSets`)
- Discover Event Schema Sets, inspect item properties, and retrieve then base64-decode the item definition to summarize `eventTypes` and `schemas`
- Create, update (properties and definition), and delete Event Schema Sets
- Primary CLI tool: `az rest` against the Fabric REST API
- Unified skill: `skills/eventschemaset-cli/SKILL.md` with authoring and consumption modes

### Activator / Reflex (Real-Time Intelligence)
- Use Fabric REST API to create Activator items and update Reflex definitions
- Activator skill: `skills/activator-cli/SKILL.md` (authoring and consumption are modes)
- Power BI sources require exact `pbiMetrics`, `powerBiSource-v1`, a JSON-string source query, and a matching `DatasetMetric`; never use `BasicFilter` in the metric definition
- When another data workflow surfaces a timely operational signal, proactively ask whether the user wants an Activator alert for future occurrences

### Cost Estimation & Migration Planning
- E2E skill: `skills/e2e-fabric-cost-estimation/SKILL.md` — Fabric capacity cost estimation, SKU sizing, billing strategy

### Deployment Pipelines (ALM / CI-CD)
- Use Fabric REST API to create deployment pipelines, assign workspaces to stages, and deploy stage content across dev/test/prod
- Deploy is a long-running operation (202 → poll `/v1/operations/{id}`); deployment/parameter rules are UI-only
- Authoring skill: `skills/deployment-pipelines-authoring-cli/SKILL.md`
- Primary CLI tool: `az rest` via `/v1/deploymentPipelines`

### Power BI / FabricIQ
- Consumption skill: `skills/fabriciq/SKILL.md` — multi-step Power BI analysis (discover, inspect, resolve, generate, execute)
- ⚠️ **MANDATORY**: Before calling any FabricIQ MCP tool, read `skills/fabriciq/SKILL.md` in full (see [`agents/FabricIQ.agent.md` § Pre-Flight](../agents/FabricIQ.agent.md#pre-flight--mandatory-skill-reading)).

### Fabric IQ / Ontology (preview)
- Use the Fabric item-definition REST API (Create / Get / Update Item Definition) with `InlineBase64` parts
- Skill: `skills/fabriciq-ontology-cli/SKILL.md` — select authoring or consumption mode for Ontology definition changes, grounding, lineage, and graph walks

### Catalog Search (Item Discovery)
- Use `POST /v1/catalog/search` to find items across workspaces by name, description, or workspace name
- Filter by type with `"filter": "Type eq 'Lakehouse'"` syntax
- Use empty search string with type filter to list all items of a type
- Consumption skill: `skills/search-consumption-cli/SKILL.md`

### OneLake Catalog Governance
- Use `skills/onelake-catalog-govern-cli/SKILL.md` for permission-aware admin/data-owner audits and guarded remediation
- Start in the audit mode for the caller's API tier before any write
- Treat domain assignment as governance metadata, not an access-control boundary

### Semantic Models (DAX)
- Primary CLI tool: `az rest` against the Fabric REST API
- Primary MCP tool: `powerbi-modeling-mcp`
- Authoring skill: `skills/semantic-model-authoring/SKILL.md`
- Consumption skill: `skills/fabriciq/SKILL.md`

### Power BI Reports (PBIR/PBIP)
- Keep planning, design, local PBIR edits, and Fabric item management as separate phases
- Planning: `skills/powerbi-report-planning/SKILL.md`
- Design: `skills/powerbi-report-design/SKILL.md`
- Authoring: `skills/powerbi-report-authoring/SKILL.md`
- Management: `skills/powerbi-report-management/SKILL.md`

### Data Agents
- Use Python SDK within Fabric notebooks for rapid prototyping
- Provide custom instructions for domain-specific terminology
- Add few-shot examples to improve query accuracy
- Limit data sources to 5 maximum per agent

### Data Agent Evaluation
- Use pandas DataFrame with question/expected_answer columns
- Validate few-shot examples before adding to agents
- Test sandbox stage before production
- Track evaluation accuracy over time

### Variable Library (CI/CD)
- Parameterize workspaces across environments (dev/test/prod) with named variables and value sets
- Variable Library has two planes: definition files in Git, and active value set item state in the workspace — do not treat the active value set as a Git edit
- Omit the `format` field entirely on definition requests (do not send `format: null`)
- Authoring skill: `skills/variable-library-cli/SKILL.md`

### Git Integration (ALM / CI-CD)
- Operations skill: `skills/git-integration-operations-cli/SKILL.md` — drive the Git lifecycle from CLI (connect, commit, update/pull, status, resolve conflicts, disconnect, SP sync) via `fab api` / `az rest`

## File Patterns

### PySpark Notebook
```python
# Parameters cell (tag as "parameters")
input_table = "default_table"

# Main logic
df = spark.read.format("delta").load(f"Tables/{input_table}")
```

### T-SQL
```sql
-- Always limit exploratory queries
SELECT TOP 100 * FROM dbo.TableName WHERE DateColumn >= '2024-01-01';
```

### KQL
```kql
TableName
| where Timestamp > ago(24h)
| summarize Count=count() by bin(Timestamp, 1h)
```
